a. Research title: "Comparative Analysis of Successful and Failed Enterprise System Implementations"

b. Case Study 1: Successful Implementation of a Boarding House Locator System

b.1. Successful Implementation of a Boarding House Locator System
A digital tool called CityStay Locator was created to make it easy for workers and students to find boarding home lodgings in Cityville, a developing university town, in response to the growing
demand for easily accessible and effective lodgings options. Before it was put into place people had to physically visit several venues or rely on word of mouth recommendationss, which was 
inefficient and time-consuming. In order to improve convenience, the system sought to digitized and centralize boarding house listings, giving users access to real-time availability, pricing,
and location-based filtering.



